                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07c055e6-ae82-3a5e-8c08-0a359918976c",
                        "entry_id": "35f1f330-7ff8-336c-8119-b556eac4707e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Staatsbürger der Ukraine"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3db2ecc7-a114-4299-9f22-9a4c5a598529",
                                "sense_id": "07c055e6-ae82-3a5e-8c08-0a359918976c",
                                "text": "Laut meinem Pass bin ich Ukrainer."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5df852d2-480a-31fa-8db1-dbd60eaabee1",
                        "entry_id": "35f1f330-7ff8-336c-8119-b556eac4707e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Angehöriger eines slawischen Volkes, das vor allem auf dem Gebiet der Ukraine und anderer ehemals sowjetischer Staaten lebt."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b948046e-c204-40c5-b9f2-de9bf2b19701",
                                "sense_id": "5df852d2-480a-31fa-8db1-dbd60eaabee1",
                                "text": "Die Ukrainer stellen die Bevölkerungsmehrheit in der Ukraine."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7250384e-6c2d-48d0-b89d-f0a1d6bb13b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "35f1f330-7ff8-336c-8119-b556eac4707e",
                        "source_sense_id": "07c055e6-ae82-3a5e-8c08-0a359918976c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürger der Ukraine",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ukrainian",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ukrainian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                        "entry_id": "474739e5-8eab-3491-ab5e-3eb3ef1d82da",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relating to Ukraine or its people or language."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bc8218d-8ed5-410c-a9c5-40132b0a4085",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "The Muſcovite, Novogrodian, and Ukrainian dialects, are the moſt uſed in Ruſſia, together with that of Archangel, which greatly reſembles the Siberian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7850b04-3b59-483d-9d4b-05a9516e59cf",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "The ukrainian peaſantry ſovv far more ſummer-grain, becauſe the vvinter-ſovving in their vvet and ſnovvleſs vvinters is apt to rot and ſo to render the harveſt doubtful, vvhich in the northern provinces is exactly the reverſe. Inſtead of the light hook-plough, they uſe the large heavy ukrainian plough, and for the horſe vvhich in Ruſſia is almoſt the only beaſt uſed for ploughing, here oxen are put to, of vvhich ſometimes eight are ſeen harneſſed to one plough."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da6754c9-dca0-4794-ac74-f38081c5b772",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "In fact, the publications of the Revolutionists which have been issued during the last three years abroad and from the secret press of St. Petersburg, present a rich source of information respecting the modern Revolutionary movement, but all these materials, being in the Russian or Ukrainian language, have scarcely contributed anything to the works written in other languages, and have remained for the most part unknown to Europe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8df65ec-8867-4793-a838-984a7c967ed2",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "The 118-foot tree grew-on the southern Ukrainian island of Khortitsa, which lies in the middle of the Dnipro River and once was home to Ukraine's largest Cossack settlement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd4b10af-7bef-4367-99d1-9d97dfa006a6",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "From Moscow on August 1, we flew down to Kiev for a quick visit to Ukraine and a meeting with Leonid Kravchuk, chairman of the Ukrainian Supreme Soviet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3981ae4-9fc6-4c08-a9c6-557e8ec7eccb",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "Everest saw a clutch of records on Thursday including the most summits for a woman and the first all-Black team – and a Ukrainian climber reached the top of the world for her war-torn country. […] The wave of summits also saw the only Ukrainian climber this season, Antonina Samoilova reach the top with her country's flag, her expedition company 14 Peaks Expedition confirmed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d2bec1f-fdb6-4e33-8f73-408cc77155d2",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "Ukraine's president on Tuesday urged Washington to recognize Russia as a state sponsor of terrorism after a missile strike on a crowded shopping mall in the central Ukrainian city of Kremenchuk killed at least 18 people."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "700a7961-6b85-4d99-beb9-b68f97619271",
                                                "sense_id": "e69d01ad-c4e8-3e0e-ba3d-f94bf2c1478a",
                                                "text": "My son, a Canada-based IT professional who often travels to Ukraine, told me about the exhilarating atmosphere on those Ukraine-bound trains, bringing home hundreds of the unwilling refugees, mostly women and children (including the babies, born in exile on the way to meet their Ukrainian fighter fathers for the first time). The difference between Ukrainian refugees and other reluctant exiles is that Ukrainians are desperate to return."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ukrainian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0621a52-8a34-35e9-b3f0-3f6704dca2d6",
                                        "entry_id": "ad806ca2-c09b-3479-a575-20f88b903363",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A citizen of Ukraine or a person of Ukrainian ethnicity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ab1f4ac-d18a-452c-a132-ec9c175c5e00",
                                                "sense_id": "d0621a52-8a34-35e9-b3f0-3f6704dca2d6",
                                                "text": "In general, it is permitted the ſubjects to utter their complaints and to make a repreſentation of them. Thus, the nobility may ſend deputies: this the Ukrainians have long been accuſtomed to do, as also the Livonians and Eſthonians: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c500c115-0ea9-4501-8b77-c0c117171bff",
                                                "sense_id": "d0621a52-8a34-35e9-b3f0-3f6704dca2d6",
                                                "text": "Zavadoffsky, a young Ukrainian, was favoured in private with the smiles of the empress [Catherine the Great]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd14723f-1fea-40a6-addd-1b13c7d36284",
                                                "sense_id": "d0621a52-8a34-35e9-b3f0-3f6704dca2d6",
                                                "text": "In western Russia, while an antipathy exists between Ukrainians and Poles, the Russian Government, by its harassing interference in religious, educational, and economical matters, has become antagonistic, not only to the Poles, but also to the Ukrainians; printing in Ukrainian is prohibited, and \"Russification\" is being carried on among Ukrainians by the same means as those employed in Poland."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07214d82-9980-4610-b3d8-175ea1bbd88e",
                                                "sense_id": "d0621a52-8a34-35e9-b3f0-3f6704dca2d6",
                                                "text": "My son, a Canada-based IT professional who often travels to Ukraine, told me about the exhilarating atmosphere on those Ukraine-bound trains, bringing home hundreds of the unwilling refugees, mostly women and children (including the babies, born in exile on the way to meet their Ukrainian fighter fathers for the first time). The difference between Ukrainian refugees and other reluctant exiles is that Ukrainians are desperate to return."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ukrainian",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f3bad71-50ab-3ee4-9885-6832f1c1daf7",
                                        "entry_id": "edd15fe6-b3a5-327f-81b8-96ddf56bbcd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The East Slavic language of Ukrainians, and the official language of Ukraine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd5b48eb-c803-4b62-9c96-6a8ec1d3be7b",
                                                "sense_id": "6f3bad71-50ab-3ee4-9885-6832f1c1daf7",
                                                "text": "It [Old Slavonic] is the root of both branches of the living Russian language: of Great Russian, which is the literary and official Russian, as well as of Ukrainian, or Southern Russian. There are, moreover, no popular dialects in our country. The fourteen millions of Ukrainians, settled in the plains of south-west Russia, all speak exactly the same language."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c8171850-fda2-4628-b8ea-98ceb2fcb3c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "35f1f330-7ff8-336c-8119-b556eac4707e",
                        "source_sense_id": "07c055e6-ae82-3a5e-8c08-0a359918976c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Staatsbürger der Ukraine",
                        "target_lang_word": "Ukrainien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Ukrainien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6aa401a0-cf0a-3cb9-89e1-b67657c100d8",
                                        "entry_id": "acde62d3-a9df-3ace-b52e-dcf9b6f96d9d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Habitant en Ukraine ou en étant originaire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c07a170-3e48-4913-8712-d4735faa6f03",
                                                "sense_id": "6aa401a0-cf0a-3cb9-89e1-b67657c100d8",
                                                "text": "Elle préférait à ces flirts les conversations intellectuelles et la camaraderie ; chaque semaine elle discutait pendant des heures à La Closerie des Lilas avec une bande d’Ukrainiens qui faisaient à Paris de vagues études ou du journalisme."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8015fc6-2358-456f-9627-7a6674ecf51a",
                                                "sense_id": "6aa401a0-cf0a-3cb9-89e1-b67657c100d8",
                                                "text": "Les partis les plus austrophiles comprennent qu'ils ont été trompés et protestent vigoureusement. C'est le cas par exemple du Bloc des Gauches du Royaume de Pologne qui est indigné et indique que le pays de Chelm comporte 66 % de Polonais contre 33,8% d’Ukrainiens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2a22e2e-7dcf-48ba-b89c-565b12ece41a",
                                                "sense_id": "6aa401a0-cf0a-3cb9-89e1-b67657c100d8",
                                                "text": "Dehors, les rachistes (contraction de Russes et fascistes) comme les surnomment désormais les Ukrainiens, tentaient de s’emparer du pays."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9dc118d4-1477-4691-a43d-cc2efbb40fc9",
                        "source_entry_id": "35f1f330-7ff8-336c-8119-b556eac4707e",
                        "source_sense_id": "07c055e6-ae82-3a5e-8c08-0a359918976c",
